ctr: single-game ("injected") mode

When the CIA has a RomFS with romfs:/manifest.cfg, load the content from
the RomFS and keep config, saves, states, core options and screenshots in
the manifest's data_dir (one flat folder per game) instead of
sdmc:/retroarch. The core info folder points at the RomFS (nothing to parse
at startup) and the bottom screen assets come from the RomFS when present.
Once the content is loaded, a bezel.png from data_dir (or the RomFS) is
shown as a full screen overlay. Stock behaviour is unchanged for CIAs
without that file.

Applies to RetroArch v1.22.2 (RETROARCH_REF in versions.env).

